cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PRIME-DS: Predictive Risk & Impurity Modeling Engine for Drug
  Substance
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this
  file) and the article listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
# ↓ 공개 직후 채우십시오
date-released: "2026-00-00"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ACCOUNT/prime-ds"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
abstract: >-
  An open-source in silico platform that generates plausible
  degradation and process-related impurities from a synthetic route
  or a formulation context and triages each generated structure
  under ICH M7(R2) with a four-layer assessment: an experimental
  record index, 23 structural alerts with four metabolic-fragment
  patterns, an ECFP4 random-forest (Q)SAR model, and read-across
  arbitration, combined under upgrade-only consensus.
keywords:
  - ICH M7
  - mutagenic impurities
  - nitrosamines
  - QSAR
  - structural alerts
  - forced degradation
  - drug-excipient compatibility
  - RDKit
